{
  "1243505": {
    "active": true,
    "expiry": "2026-11-03",
    "notes": "deepmerge mergeObject() allows prototype poisoning of returned objects (GHSA-gcqx-w48m-w2h4), low severity. Every published release from 4.2.0 through the latest 4.3.1 is affected, so no patched release exists. Reaches the tree only through dev tooling (jest -> @jest/core -> jest-config -> deepmerge): npm ls deepmerge --omit=dev is empty, so nothing is shipped in the production bundle."
  },
  "1244012": {
    "active": true,
    "expiry": "2026-11-13",
    "notes": "minimatch globparts amplification denial of service (GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249), moderate, published 2026-10-30. Range is every release below 11.0.1; the tree holds 3.1.5, 9.0.9 and 10.2.6 through eslint, jest, typescript-eslint and markdownlint-cli, and every legacy-v* backport tag predates the advisory, so no patched release exists on those lines. npm ls minimatch --omit=dev is empty, so nothing ships. The expiry forces a re-check for backports."
  },
  "1244013": {
    "active": true,
    "expiry": "2026-11-13",
    "notes": "glob AbortSignal cancellation bypass (GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4), moderate, published 2026-10-30. Range is 9.0.0 through 14.0.1, first patched in 14.0.2 on the 14 line only; the tree holds 10.5.0 and 13.0.6 through jest, rimraf and Storybook's docgen plugin, and legacy-v10 is 10.5.0, so no patched release exists on those lines. npm ls glob --omit=dev is empty, so nothing ships. The expiry forces a re-check for backports."
  }
